<title>MOROCCO: African Bank lends Morocco $82.5 mln for railway.</title>
<headline>African Bank lends Morocco $82.5 mln for railway.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The African Development Bank said on Thursday it has loaned Morocco $82.5 million to extend and upgrade its 2,000 km (1,250 miles) railway network.</p>
<p>In a statement, the bank said the loan &quot;aimed at improving the network services and transportation capacity,&quot; in the North African country.</p>
<p>The World Bank said earlier that it would contribute $85 million to expand Morocco's railway and modernise its locomotives and coaches.</p>
<p>($1= 9.3 dirhams)</p>
<p>- Rabat newsroom +212-7 72 65 18</p>
</text>
